Modifications (GPLv3 section 5(a))
----------------------------------
This work was forked from the upstream project and modified by the NearBird
maintainers. The NearBird fork was created on 2026-10-07 (commit 8d7de5e7,
"chore: import BitChat Android foundation"). Changes made after that date
include, among others: the NearBird name, application ID and release
pipeline; the opt-in "Internet features" gate; a durable message outbox with
delivery retry; encrypted on-device conversation storage; log redaction; the
open-source licences screen; and this documentation.

The complete, dated record of every modification is the git history of this
repository: https://github.com/Rohanr1904/MeshUp (the repository may be renamed
to NearBird; GitHub redirects the old name). Use `git log --follow <file>` to
see the changes and dates for any single file.

Wire compatibility
------------------
NearBird deliberately keeps the upstream wire-protocol identifiers (packet
formats, Bluetooth service UUIDs, the "bitchat://" link scheme and similar) so
that it can interoperate with existing bitchat clients. These identifiers are
technical compatibility labels. They do not mean that NearBird is endorsed by,
or is the same product as, bitchat.

